      "issues": null,
      "text": "[SECTION: Executive Summary] The pilot tests if AI Tutor can provide more timely, personalized business-case reasoning feedback than existing study methods for MBA students.\n[SECTION: Problem] The proposed pilot tests a demand hypothesis that students need more timely, personalized business-case reasoning feedback.\n[SECTION: Target Customer] Business graduate students seeking timely, personalized business-case reasoning feedback; business-school instructors are potential institutional buyers.\n[SECTION: Market Opportunity] US adults aged 18+ enrolled/applying to MBA programs; potential institutional buyers are business-school instructors.\n[SECTION: Solution] An English-language AI case-coaching service with guided questions, evidence-aware feedback, and practice with licensed or openly reusable cases.\n[SECTION: Value Proposition] Personalized, timely business-case reasoning feedback for MBA students.\n[SECTION: Competitor Analysis] Competitor: Khanmigo AI tutoring service with personalized coaching, district tools, and professional learning.\n[SECTION: Business Model] AI-driven tutoring service for MBA students and potential institutional buyers (business schools).\n[SECTION: Go-to-Market Strategy] Target US adults 18+ enrolled/applying to MBA programs; sell directly to students and pitch to business-school instructors.\n[SECTION: Financial Assumptions] Scenario meaning: The pilot tests if AI Tutor can provide more timely, personalized business-case reasoning feedback than existing study methods for MBA students. Risk: Uncertainty around adoption, cost-effectiveness, and learning impact. Decision: Based on low-end deterministic values, the pilot may not be financially viable (monthly loss of $6,000, ending cash of $30,000, break-even at 500 users).\n[SECTION: Risks and Mitigations] Uncertainty around adoption, cost-effectiveness, and learning impact. Mitigation: Conduct pilot to validate demand hypothesis and refine business model.\n[SECTION: Implementation Roadmap] Conduct pilot, validate demand hypothesis, refine business model, scale if successful.\n[SECTION: Appendix] None",
